{#- How a ticket of an older record schema is brought to the current one, stated once as the
    macro `rule` and called by both places `follow-up-task.md.j2` may copy such a ticket: the
    re-dispatch section, and the feedback mode's step that edits the ticket a quoted comment
    asks to change. A comment asking for a change to a schema-5 ticket once ended at
    `board-status`'s schema refusal, its reply posted and its issue left stale, because only
    the re-dispatch carried this rule. The schemas and headings it names are the module's,
    through `shape`, and `tests/test_follow_up_tickets.py` holds them to it. It is imported at
    the head of that template rather than included where it is used, so every mode loads it
    at one point: the store records a rendering's template digest in the order its templates
    load, and `onepipeline template check` recomputes it in one fixed order.
-#}
<!-- llmlint: ignore-block[changed_behavior_has_e2e] Each clause is the agent's instruction for an edit the suite never scripts a verdict for — which fields a ticket already carries and what its evidence supports are its reading of the tree — so a journey can only drive the tooling around it, and does: `tests/plan_tooling/test_follow_ups_recipe_e2e.py`'s `test_a_feedback_re_dispatch_brings_a_schema_4_ticket_to_one_fix_updating_its_item` brings schema-4 tickets forward with the `## Repository` section removed, the options moved under `## Rejected fixes`, and `host` and `repositories` recorded, and `tests/plan_tooling/test_follow_ups_comment_answers_e2e.py` drives the rule in the feedback mode over schemas 4, 5 and 6 and another run's schema-6 item. Schemas 1 to 3 meet the same `validate` refusal those do, which `tests/test_follow_up_tickets.py` holds for schemas 1, 2, 3, 4 and 6; its `test_a_schema_9_ticket_of_this_run_brought_forward_validates_at_schema_10` drives a schema-9 ticket through `board-status` to schema 10, refused until its `## Root cause` and `## Duplicate search` are written, and the comment-answers journey brings a schema-9 ticket forward beside the others. -->
{% macro rule(shape, board, board_status, re_estimate) -%}
- a ticket of an older schema is brought to the current shape before it is copied, its
  `repositories` listing every repository its fix changes, its `host` read from this machine
  with `hostname`, and its `## {{ shape.impact }}` section written from the evidence the ticket
  already carries, re-verifying only a claim that no longer holds; its `## {{ shape.retired_headings[0] }}`
  section removed, any path the ticket still needs moved into `## Root cause`; its
  `## {{ shape.retired_headings[1] }}` rewritten as `## {{ shape.suggested_fix }}`, stating the one fix the ticket's
  evidence supports; and every other option it offered moved into `## {{ shape.rejected_fixes }}`,
  with why each was not chosen; then it is validated once `{{ board_status }}` has written its
  estimate, as the rule below states.
- a ticket of this run older than schema {{ shape.structure_at }} is brought to it by writing its
  `## {{ shape.impact }}` prose as its labelled parts, {{ shape.impact_parts }}, from the evidence it already
  carries, with both severities judged again by the rubric — an acceptable workaround
  lowers a severity above `low`, and one too costly to lower it is `{{ shape.no_workaround }}` — and its
  `## {{ shape.suggested_fix }}` as one opening paragraph and its unit subsections, headed
  {{ shape.unit_heading }}; then `{{ board_status }} --board {{ board }} <path of the ticket>` records it at
  schema {{ shape.schema }}. A schema-{{ shape.unestimated_schema }} ticket also records its `{{ shape.frequency_field }}` from that evidence first, and
  `{{ board_status }}` writes its `{{ shape.estimate_field }}`, its `## {{ shape.impact }}` estimate line and its
  `{{ shape.priority_field }}`, reading its schema-{{ shape.unestimated_schema }} board item as storing no estimate; validate it and
  copy it. Another run's schema-{{ shape.unestimated_schema }} item is brought to schema {{ shape.estimate_at }} by `{{ re_estimate }} --board {{ board }} <its
  id>` alone, and only when this run adds or edits its evidence comment there, or posts a
  reply there marked `verdict="{{ shape.confirms }}"`; another run's item of schema {{ shape.estimate_at }} or later keeps its
  schema, and its body is that run's to restructure.
- a ticket of this run older than schema {{ shape.invariant_at }} is brought to it when this run rewrites it:
  its `## Root cause` is written as its labelled parts, {{ shape.root_cause_parts }}, from the
  evidence it already carries; its dependency entries and the related items it mentions become
  the entries of a `## {{ shape.related_tickets }}` section, {{ shape.related_shape }}, left out when there are
  none; and it closes with `## {{ shape.duplicate_search }}`, which says that no search was recorded when it
  was filed where this dispatch ran none for it — a bound ticket runs none. Then
  `{{ board_status }}` records it at schema {{ shape.schema }}; validate it and copy it. Another run's item
  keeps its schema and its body.
{%- endmacro %}
<!-- llmlint: ignore-end[changed_behavior_has_e2e] -->
